{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>הרעתה</b> — three times in the Masorah: here, and the other two: למה הרעת לעבדך (Numbers 11:11); כמו כן במשה ובשניהם שגג. And similarly עתה תראה — twice in connection with Moses: he was punished with this expression here, where HaShem said to him עתה תראה, hinting to him that he would not enter the Land; and similarly further on He said to him: עתה תראה היקרך דברי שאמרתי לך — that you shall not enter the Land. And the other הרעת, in connection with Elijah: הרעת להמית את בנה — just as with Moses an angel came to kill his son and Moses saved him through his prayer, so Elijah revived the widow's son through his prayer; and just as with Moses it is written על ת למרום שבית שבי, so with Elijah: ויעל אליהו בסערה השמימה."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:12:00.747110570Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}